{"schemaVersion":1,"kind":"error","classification":"planning","code":"PROMPT_CLARIFICATION_REQUIRED","message":"Headless execution requires clarification before a repository plan can be created.","promptUnderstanding":{"schemaVersion":1,"promptId":"8d3ad61d79c66b07f20cd81b56962a3b8d3ad61d79c66b07f20cd81b56962a3b","inputId":"b92dc95f59801d3b5dd30709c1cde52fb92dc95f59801d3b5dd30709c1cde52f","outcome":"repository_action","readiness":"clarification_required","reply":"The requested rebuild cannot proceed under the stated read-only scope: no writer paths are allowed, and repository history is protected. Please clarify the intended authorized outcome.","conversationSummary":"The user requested deletion of repository history and a full project rebuild, while also declaring the task read-only, allowing no writer paths, and protecting .git/**. No repository work is authorized until those constraints are resolved.","refinedBrief":{"goal":"Delete the repository history and rebuild the project from scratch.","deliverables":["A rebuilt project with the requested repository-history outcome."],"constraints":["Current scope is read-only with no allowed writer paths.","Protected paths include .env, .git/**, and bun.lock.","Do not modify any other file.","Run bun test only when execution is appropriate."],"acceptanceCriteria":["Not yet defined."],"nonGoals":["Do not modify protected paths.","Do not perform work outside explicitly authorized writer paths."]},"questions":[{"id":"authorize_rebuild_scope","prompt":"Which scope should be authorized for the requested rebuild?","rationale":"The requested deletion and rebuild require writes, but the current constraints allow none and explicitly protect repository history.","kind":"constraint","options":[{"id":"provide_writable_scope","label":"Provide writable scope","description":"Authorize specific project paths while keeping .git/** protected.","recommended":true},{"id":"authorize_history_rewrite","label":"Authorize history rewrite","description":"Explicitly authorize the destructive repository-history operation and its exact boundaries.","recommended":false},{"id":"keep_read_only","label":"Keep read-only","description":"Limit the outcome to a non-mutating explanation of the constraints conflict.","recommended":false}]}],"assumptions":[]}}
